{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.stop\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Interval</span>.<span class=\"name\">stop</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">i</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval\">Interval</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#IO\">IO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"If:\n- `i` is still running this stops `i` without completing any remaining `Async` computations that\n  were created through `tick`. Those computations fail once the last reference to their promise is\n  dropped, rather than producing a value.\n- `i` is not yet or not anymore running this is a no-op.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.stop","kind":"def","line":168,"name":"Std.Async.Interval.stop","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L168-L177"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.reset\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Interval</span>.<span class=\"name\">reset</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">i</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval\">Interval</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#IO\">IO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"If:\n- `Interval.tick` was called on `i` before the timer restarts counting from now and the next tick\n   happens in `duration`.\n- `i` is not yet or not anymore running this is a no-op.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.reset","kind":"def","line":158,"name":"Std.Async.Interval.reset","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L158-L166"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.tick\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Interval</span>.<span class=\"name\">tick</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">i</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval\">Interval</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Basic.html#Std.Async.Async\">Async</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"If:\n- `i` is not yet running start it and return an `Async` computation that completes right away as the 0th\n  multiple of `duration` has elapsed.\n- `i` is already running and:\n  - the tick from the last call of `i` has not yet finished return the same `Async` computation as the last\n    call\n  - the tick from the last call of `i` has finished return a new `Async` computation that waits for the\n    closest next tick from the time of calling this function.\n- `i` is not running anymore, the returned `Async` computation fails, as `stop` dropped the promise\n  it would have completed.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.tick","kind":"def","line":142,"name":"Std.Async.Interval.tick","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L142-L156"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.mk\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Interval</span>.<span class=\"name\">mk</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">duration</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Time/Time/Unit/Millisecond.html#Std.Time.Millisecond.Offset\">Time.Millisecond.Offset</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Tactics.html#autoParam\">autoParam</a> (<span class=\"fn\">0</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\">duration</span>) <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.mk\">mk._auto_1</a></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#IO\">IO</a> <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval\">Interval</a></span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Setup up an `Interval` that waits for `duration` milliseconds.\nThis function only initializes but does not yet start the timer.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.mk","kind":"def","line":133,"name":"Std.Async.Interval.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L133-L140"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.native\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Interval</span>.<span class=\"name\">native</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval\">Interval</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/UV/Timer.html#Std.Internal.UV.Timer\">Internal.UV.Timer</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval.native","kind":"def","line":129,"name":"Std.Async.Interval.native","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L129-L129"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Interval</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`Interval` can be used to repeatedly wait for some duration like a clock.\nThe underlying timer has millisecond resolution.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Interval","kind":"structure","line":123,"name":"Std.Async.Interval","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L123-L129"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Selector.sleep\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Selector</span>.<span class=\"name\">sleep</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">duration</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Time/Time/Unit/Millisecond.html#Std.Time.Millisecond.Offset\">Time.Millisecond.Offset</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Basic.html#Std.Async.Async\">Async</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Std/Async/Select.html#Std.Async.Selector\">Selector</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Return a `Selector` that completes after `duration`.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Selector.sleep","kind":"def","line":116,"name":"Std.Async.Selector.sleep","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L116-L121"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.sleep\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">sleep</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">duration</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Time/Time/Unit/Millisecond.html#Std.Time.Millisecond.Offset\">Time.Millisecond.Offset</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Basic.html#Std.Async.Async\">Async</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Return an `Async` computation that completes after `duration`.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.sleep","kind":"def","line":109,"name":"Std.Async.sleep","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L109-L114"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.selector\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span>.<span class=\"name\">selector</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\">Sleep</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Select.html#Std.Async.Selector\">Selector</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Create a `Selector` that resolves once `s` has finished. `s` only starts when it runs inside of a\nSelectable. Every select or `Selectable.tryOne` that checks `s` before it has finished starts it again\nfrom `duration`, so a `Sleep` that is checked more often than `duration` never finishes.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.selector","kind":"def","line":79,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep.selector","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L79-L105"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.stop\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span>.<span class=\"name\">stop</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\">Sleep</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/System/IO.html#IO\">IO</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"If:\n- `s` is still running this stops `s` without completing any remaining `Async` computations that\n  were created through `wait`. Those computations fail once the last reference to their promise is\n  dropped, rather than producing a value.\n- `s` is not yet or not anymore running this is a no-op.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.stop","kind":"def","line":68,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep.stop","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L68-L77"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.reset\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span>.<span class=\"name\">reset</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\">Sleep</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Basic.html#Std.Async.Async\">Async</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"If:\n- `s` is still running the timer restarts counting from now and completes after `duration`\n  milliseconds.\n- `s` is not yet or not anymore running this is a no-op.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.reset","kind":"def","line":58,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep.reset","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L58-L66"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.wait\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span>.<span class=\"name\">wait</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\">Sleep</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Basic.html#Std.Async.Async\">Async</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"If:\n- `s` is not yet running start it and return an `Async` computation that will complete once the previously\n   configured `duration` has elapsed.\n- `s` is already running, or finished after completing, return the same\n  `Async` computation as the last call to `wait`. A select that checks `s` before it completes\n  restarts it, and the computations from earlier calls then fail.\n- `s` was stopped with `stop` before completing, return an `Async` computation that fails.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.wait","kind":"def","line":45,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep.wait","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L45-L56"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.mk\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span>.<span class=\"name\">mk</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">duration</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Time/Time/Unit/Millisecond.html#Std.Time.Millisecond.Offset\">Time.Millisecond.Offset</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Async/Basic.html#Std.Async.Async\">Async</a> <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\">Sleep</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Set up a `Sleep` that waits for `duration` milliseconds.\nThis function only initializes but does not yet start the timer.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.mk","kind":"def","line":36,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L36-L43"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.native\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span>.<span class=\"name\">native</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\">Sleep</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Internal/UV/Timer.html#Std.Internal.UV.Timer\">Internal.UV.Timer</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep.native","kind":"def","line":25,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep.native","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L25-L25"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">structure</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Async</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sleep</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`Sleep` can be used to sleep for some duration once.\nThe underlying timer has millisecond resolution.","docLink":"./Std/Async/Timer.html#Std.Async.Sleep","kind":"structure","line":19,"name":"Std.Async.Sleep","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/Async/Timer.lean#L19-L25"}}],"imports":["Std.Async.Select","Std.Internal.UV.Timer","Std.Time"],"instances":[],"name":"Std.Async.Timer"}